Found while writing the consumer skill perl-www-hetzner (p5-www-hetzner k35); each checked against WWW::Hetzner lib/:

- servers->list and servers->list_by_label fetch one page; list_all(%filters) follows every page. One-page calls: lib/OCP/Provider/Hetzner.pm line 115 (the idempotency lookup) and line 421 (list_servers_by_cluster, used by sweeps), lib/OCP/Cmd/Hetzner/List.pm lines 33-34. A cluster with more servers than one page misses servers there.
- lib/OCP/Hetzner/Picker.pm lines 14 and 18 read locations->list and server_types->list, also one page each.
- Picker.pm line 42 hides deprecated types with !$_->deprecated. The API drops the top-level deprecated field; the attribute then reads undef and the filter hides nothing. ServerType->locations (WWW::Hetzner 0.102, already pinned) carries name, available and deprecated per location.

Done when: those reads use list_all (servers with label_selector), the picker offers a type for a location only when that location entry is available and not deprecated, and tests drive both through a fake IO with a second page.

